# Q22 round 2: replace Q22a,b,c,e,f in /output/report.json by the shared-envelope joint-fit versions (Q22d, the CO-floor test of round 1, is kept). Idempotent.
import json
R=json.load(open('/output/report.json'))
R['results']=[x for x in R['results'] if not (x['quantity'].startswith('Q22') and x['quantity'][3:4] in 'abcef')]
R['recipe']=[x for x in R['recipe'] if 'Q22 round 2' not in x['description']]
R['datasets']=[x for x in R['datasets'] if 'Q22 round 2' not in x.get('role','')]
A=[{"name":"model","value":"JOINT N+S fit (32 data, scripts/q22b_shared.py): separate cores per nucleus (T,n,N_HCN,N_HCO+, filling inside the Gaussian core, 0.24 arcsec T_b tied, Q22 round-1 likelihoods) + ONE shared extended zone (same T,n,N,filling at both nuclei; env 'sh'); variants: 'shf' shared T,n,N but separate fillings; 'sep' independent envelopes; 'same' = each nucleus single state (envelope has the own core's T,n,N, own filling); 'shH' = shared with Tc 10-25 K, Te 50-150 K; 'none' cores only. Each 10 arcsec aperture = own core + 0.5x the other nucleus' core (aperture edge; 0 and 1 tested) + envelope. LAMDA RADEX LVG, dv 150 km/s, Tbg 2.73 K (5 K variant). Tempered SMC, 12000 particles, 4 seeds (3 for sensitivity runs); evidence = mean lnZ over seeds, seed sd 0.4-1.1 (up to 2.9 at k=22)."},
 {"name":"data","value":"1.7 arcsec deblended ladders + Tint (as round 1) and the six team-b p0028 10 arcsec intensities per nucleus (same underlying maps; 10 arcsec flux scale per band per nucleus, sigma 10%, 30% in the sg30 variant). The 10 arcsec apertures are not independent data of the 1.7 arcsec ones; no uv-matched re-imaging was done."},
 {"name":"priors","value":"flat in log T 10-150 K (prior P(T>=50)=0.41); flat-in-T variant by importance reweighting (prior P(T>=50)=0.71); log n 3-8, log N 13-18.5, log filling -3..0; n_env<n_core"}]
def res(q,t,v,u,un,c,e):
    R['results'].append({"quantity":q,"target":t,"value":v,"uncertainty":u,"unit":un,"assumptions":A,"confidence":c,"evidence":e})
EV="scripts/q22b_shared.py, q22b_runone.sh, q22b_jobs.txt, q22b_post.py, build_report_q22b.py -> out/q22b/runs/*, q22b_summary.csv, q22b_PT.csv, q22b_mass.csv, post.log"
res("Q22a: joint N+S model comparison: one SHARED extended zone + separate cores (chi2 14.1, k=17, lnZ -52.5, BIC 73) beats independent envelopes (k=22, lnZ -60.9, dlnZ +8.5, BIC 91) and beats 'each nucleus a single state' (lnZ -77.3, dlnZ +24.9, chi2 62.6 mostly N 52) and cores only (chi2 133); the N single-state rejection survives envelope sharing and cross-nucleus leakage but rests on the combination of HCN and HCO+ 10 arcsec lines",
 "N, S (1.7 + 10 arcsec, 32 data)",
 "Base run (Tbg 2.73 K, 4 seeds; chi2 = profile minimum over final particles; k free params; lnZ mean [seed sd]): cores only k=12 chi2 132.7 lnZ -118.3[0.9] BIC 174; same-state per nucleus k=14 62.6 (N 52.3, S 10.2) -77.3[0.7] BIC 111; shared envelope sh k=17 14.1 (N 8.3, S 5.7) -52.5[0.7] BIC 73.0; sh with separate fillings k=18 15.7 -54.4[1.1] BIC 78; independent envelopes sep k=22 15.1 (N 10.7, S 4.4) -60.9[1.1] BIC 91.4; hypothesis shH (Tc 10-25, Te 50-150 K) k=17 14.0 -49.9[0.8] BIC 73.0. => shared envelope vs independent: dlnZ +8.5, dBIC -18 (same data fitted with 5 fewer parameters at equal chi2: the independent envelopes double-count the same gas). Single-state-per-nucleus (the Q20 picture extended to 10 arcsec) vs shared envelope: dlnZ +24.9 in the base run. Sensitivity of this dlnZ(sh - same): Tbg 5 K +26.0; 10 arcsec scale sigma 30%: +26.1; other-core weight 0 / 1: +26.8 / +17.9; drop 10 arcsec 4-3: +24.1; drop 2-1: +24.0; drop all HCN 10 arcsec: +5.5 (chi2 same 20.9 vs 11.2); drop all HCO+ 10 arcsec: +4.8; leave one line out (HCN 2-1,3-2,4-3, HCO+ 2-1,3-2,4-3): +25.0/+17.7/+21.9/+25.0/+19.5/+21.3. So no single line or flux scale produces the second state; but once one whole species is removed the preference falls to dlnZ ~5 (about 3 sigma-equivalent), i.e. it is carried by the HCN-vs-HCO+ pattern of the 10 arcsec lines vs the 1.7 arcsec ladders together. Independent-envelope variants (sep) fit equally well with free 10 arcsec scales (sg30: chi2 9.6) and the shared model remains preferred in every variant (dlnZ vs sep 3-10). The N rather than S origin: same-state chi2(N)=52 vs chi2(S)=10; round-1 per-nucleus result (dlnZ +23 at N, +2.9 for S) is therefore reproduced with the other nucleus' core leaked in.",
 "lnZ seed sd 0.4-1.1 (4 seeds); profile chi2 from best of final particles (+-1)","chi2, k, lnZ, BIC","medium",EV)
res("Q22b: prior-robust P(T) of the extended zone with ONE shared envelope: Te = 53 [34,78] K (log-T prior) / 56 [39,78] K (linear-T prior); P(Te>=50) = 0.55 / 0.63 vs prior 0.41 / 0.71, i.e. NOT evidence for a hot (>=50 K) envelope; at Tbg 5 K or with separate fillings P(Te>=50)=0.18-0.21; the envelope is warmer than both cores with P~0.9 (Tbg 2.73 K)",
 "N, S, shared extended zone",
 "Posterior medians [16,84], Tbg 2.73 K, shared envelope (4 seeds pooled): Te=52.8 [33.9,77.8] K (flat log T), 56.4 [38.8,78.5] (flat T). P(Te>=50)=0.55 (log prior; prior 0.41) / 0.63 (linear prior; prior 0.71 -> the data push DOWN relative to this prior). P(Te>=30)=0.89/0.95, P(Te>=100)=0.04. Seed-to-seed range of P(Te>=50) 0.16-0.55 (2-seed trial runs) and 0.09-0.80 across the sensitivity variants (drop/leave-out/other-core weight), so the hot fraction is unconstrained by the data. Tbg 5 K: Te=35 [25,51] K, P(Te>=50)=0.18 (log)/0.21 (lin). Separate fillings (shf): Te 39 [25,52], P=0.19/0.20. Independent envelopes (sep): Te_N 35 [26,48], Te_S 37 [24,62], P(Te>=50)=0.14/0.28 (log). Imposed hypothesis shH (Tc 10-25, Te 50-150 K): Te 69 [56,93] K, Tc_N 16.7 [12,22], Tc_S 16.0 [13,21], chi2 14.0 (identical to the free fit) and lnZ -49.9 (+2.6 over the free fit through prior volume): allowed, not required. Ordered pair: P(Te>Tc_N)=0.90, P(Te>Tc_S)=0.90 (Tbg 2.73 K; 0.60/0.79 at Tbg 5 K; 0.66/0.84 with the linear-T prior); corr(lg Te, lg Tc_S)=-0.28 (hotter envelope <-> cooler core). Core temperatures (not labelled by envelope/core swap because Te is a separate parameter): Tc_N=16 [12,32] K, Tc_S=20.5 [13.5,32] K (Tbg 5 K: N 30 [19,66], S 19 [13,36]); P(Tc_N>=Tc_S)=0.41; the S core value is the cool 17-25 K core of Q20 and N-S core temperature difference is not significant. Envelope: n=10^4.4 [10^4.0,10^4.8], N_HCN=10^15.1 [10^14.5,10^15.9], filling 0.26 [0.10,0.59] (10 arcsec), tau32(HCN)<~1. Cores: eta_core N 0.43, S 0.28; n_c 10^6.1 (N), 10^6.3 (S); N_HCN core 10^16.4 (N), 10^15.8 (S). Round-1 values (Te 68 [38,106], P=0.71 for S alone; N 72, 0.72) came from independent envelopes and are superseded.",
 "16-84% over pooled SMC posteriors; prior sensitivity shown","K / probability","medium",EV)
res("Q22c: N versus S and consistency with p0041: the HCN/HCO+ N-S contrast is carried by the N core (single-state N rejected) but the temperatures of cores and shared envelope do not differ significantly between N and S; N core posterior is low-T/high-n with a Tbg-dependent hot branch, in line with the bimodal Tk of p0041",
 "N vs S",
 "Same-state per nucleus: chi2(N)=52, chi2(S)=10 -> a second (extended, lower-density, tau~1) zone is needed for N; S is fitted by a single state in the 1.7 arcsec+10 arcsec data when its own envelope is allowed (round 1) but with the shared envelope both nuclei need the common extended zone (sh is preferred over 'same' by dlnZ +25 jointly, the N part carrying most of it). Tc_N 16 [12,32] vs Tc_S 20.5 [13.5,32] K: P(Tc_N>=Tc_S)=0.41 (log prior), 0.57 (linear prior), 0.73 at Tbg 5 K, i.e. no N-S difference; Tc_N at Tbg 5 K is 30 [19,66] K, wide and sensitive to the background temperature, as is the p0041 N posterior (bimodal: Tk at its 300 K cap vs cold/dense branch; N(HCN)/N(HCO+) excess only ~2 sigma). In the present fit N has N_HCO+/N_HCN(core)=0.1 vs S ~7 at core level (HCN-rich N core; HCO+-rich S core), which is the same direction as p0041's HCN/HCO+ excess at N, but the column-ratio is poorly constrained (N(HCN)c 10^16.4 [10^16.2,10^17.0] vs N(HCO+)c 10^15.4 [10^15.2,10^16.0] at N; N 10^15.8 vs 10^16.6 at S) and should be read with p0041's ~2 sigma caveat; no claim of chemical difference is made. The CO floor test of round 1 (Q22d) is unchanged. Temperature labels: because Te is an independent parameter and the cores' T posteriors are listed per nucleus, no 'core/envelope' label swapping occurs in the joint fit; the swap seen in round 1 at Tbg 5 K in independent M2 fits is a feature of the unshared model.",
 "see Q22b","dimensionless","low-medium",EV)
res("Q22e: mass fractions and abundance constraints from the shared-envelope fit: core mass fraction of the HCN-traced gas within 10 arcsec = 0.009 [0.003,0.05] (S) and 0.08 [0.02,0.39] (N), independent of X(HCN) but proportional to the assumed envelope area; M_core(S) <= Mdyn(0.58e8) needs X(HCN) >~ 4e-9; the cores are clumpy (path 0.1-1 pc at X=1e-8, filling <0.02 of 66 pc)",
 "N, S",
 "Conventions: mu=2.8 m_H, D=40 Mpc (194 pc/arcsec), X(HCN)=N_HCN/N_H2 equal in cores and envelope, core area pi*(FWHM/2)^2 with pedestal-inclusive HCN 3-2 FWHM 0.455 (S)/0.507 (N) arcsec x core filling; envelope = filling x pi*(5 arcsec)^2 (one 10 arcsec circle; the N and S apertures overlap, the shared envelope is counted once per aperture). Shared envelope (median): X=1e-9/3e-9/1e-8/3e-8: M_core(S)=2.3e8/7.8e7/2.3e7/7.8e6 Msun, M_core(N)=1.9e9/6.3e8/1.9e8/6.3e7, M_env(10 arcsec)=1.8e10/6.1e9/1.8e9/6.1e8; core fraction S 0.009 [0.003,0.053], N 0.084 [0.017,0.39] (independent-envelope fit: S 0.023 [0.006,0.10], N 0.076 [0.018,0.52]). Core path length N_H2/n: S 1.0/0.33/0.10/0.03 pc, N 9.8/3.3/1.0/0.33 pc for X=1e-9..3e-8 (independent: S 11/3.6/1.1/0.36, N 23/7.7/2.3/0.77): all << the 50-66 pc core size, so the nuclei are not uniform space-filling HCN clouds but ensembles of dense clumps (filling factor along the line of sight L/66 pc ~ 0.002-0.15 at X=1e-8..1e-9, over and above eta_core); this is a constraint on clumping rather than on temperature. Fraction of the posterior with L_core<=66 pc and L_env<=500 pc: S 0.84/0.94/0.99/1.0, N 0.90/0.98/1.0/1.0 (shared; X as above). Self-consistency with Mdyn(S, 48 pc)=0.58e8 (Q5f): P(M_core<=Mdyn) = 0.09/0.39/0.74/0.91 for X=1e-9/3e-9/1e-8/3e-8 (shared; 0.02/0.15/0.52/0.84 independent), so X(HCN)>~4e-9 (shared; >~1e-8 independent) is needed for the core not to exceed the dynamical mass; the round-1 M_core(S)=1.5e8 at X=1e-8 was a consequence of the independent-envelope fit and a larger eta*N core. M_env(10 arcsec) at X=1e-9 (1.8e10) is of order or above the total molecular gas of the system and X<~2e-9 is disfavoured on that ground (CO-based total mass not re-derived here, no CO-derived mass in the team forum). The mass fractions scale with the adopted envelope area (10 arcsec circle); with a larger area the core fraction falls proportionally. H13CN(4-3) test: unchanged from round 1 (S consistent with HCN/H13CN>4 for R>=30 in 54-90%; N needs 12C/13C>~50-100).",
 "median [16,84] given in the value text; 4 seeds pooled","Msun, pc, dimensionless","low-medium",EV)
res("Q22f: verdict (round 2): a joint two-component model (cool 12-32 K cores + one shared extended zone, Te=53 [34,78] K) fits the 1.7 and 10 arcsec ladders (chi2 14 for 32 data, k=17) far better than the single-phase core of Q20 (chi2 133) and than a single state per nucleus (dlnZ +25, driven by N), but the data do not require the envelope to be hot (P(Te>=50)=0.2-0.6, prior-dependent; Tc_S=20 [14,32] K as in Q20)",
 "N, S",
 "Summary: (1) cores only cannot fit 10 arcsec (chi2 133, chi2 of the 10 arcsec lines alone 24-28 per nucleus). (2) The shared envelope removes the double counting of independent envelopes (dlnZ +8.5 over independent, 5 fewer parameters, same chi2). (3) The single-state alternative is rejected by dlnZ +18..+26 in every sensitivity variant except when a whole species is dropped (+5): 10 arcsec flux-scale sigma 30%, other-core weight 0/1, Tbg 5 K, dropping 4-3 or 2-1, leave-one-line-out; a separate second T is not required, a second (lower-density, lower-column, filling ~0.26) zone is. (4) The temperature of that zone is poorly constrained: 53 [34,78] K at Tbg 2.73 K, 35 [25,51] K at Tbg 5 K; P(Te>=50) 0.55/0.18 (prior 0.41), 0.63/0.21 (linear-T prior; prior 0.71); the hypothesis of the item (Tc 10-25 K, Te>=50 K) fits as well as the free model (chi2 14.0 vs 14.1) and is not excluded, but is not demanded. (5) Cores: Tc 16 [12,32] (N), 20.5 [13.5,32] (S) K, the Q20 17-25 K S core is recovered; N-S difference not significant. (6) Cores hold 1-10% of the HCN-traced mass within 10 arcsec and have path lengths <<66 pc at X>=1e-9: clumpy cores. Still open: uv-matched (tapered) re-imaging of 10 arcsec ladders for N, S and midpoint (current 10 arcsec numbers are team-b p0028 values, one flux scale per band), IR-pumping Tbg, X(HCN) from H13CN with deeper data, dense-gas fraction from independent CO mass.",
 "see Q22a-e","dimensionless","medium",EV)
R['recipe'].append({"order":max(x['order'] for x in R['recipe'])+1,"stage":"statistical_analysis","description":"Q22 round 2: q22b_shared.py joint N+S non-LTE fit with ONE shared extended zone, separate cores, other-nucleus core leakage into the 10 arcsec apertures; envelope variants sh/shf/sep/same/shH/none; sensitivity: 10 arcsec scale 30%, cross weight 0/1, drop 4-3 / 2-1 / HCN / HCO+ 10 arcsec, leave-one-line-out, Tbg 5 K; 12000-particle tempered SMC, 3-4 seeds; q22b_post.py: P(T) under log and linear T priors, evidence tables, masses; build_report_q22b.py","scripts":["scripts/q22b_shared.py","scripts/q22b_runone.sh","scripts/q22b_jobs.txt","scripts/q22b_post.py","scripts/build_report_q22b.py"],"software":"numpy, scipy, pandas, RADEX grids"})
R['datasets'].append({"files":["out/q4c/grid4_hcn.npz","out/q4c/grid4_hco+.npz","out/q1/q1_deblend_ladders_xb4f.csv","out/q4b/dilution.csv"],"content":"RADEX grids, 1.7 arcsec deblended ladders, 0.24 arcsec T_b/sizes, team-b p0028 10 arcsec intensities","role":"Q22 round 2 joint shared-envelope fit"})
R['caveats']=[c for c in R['caveats'] if not c.startswith('Q22: (a)')]
R['caveats'].append("Q22 (round 2): (a) the 10 arcsec ladders are team-b p0028 values, not matched in uv/beam to the 1.7 arcsec data, one flux scale per band per nucleus; (b) the aperture-overlap treatment assumes the other core contributes 0.5x (edge of aperture; 0 and 1 tested) and a single shared uniform envelope; (c) uniform-sphere RADEX zones, one line width, X(HCN) equal in core and envelope; masses scale with the assumed 10 arcsec envelope area and 1/X; (d) P(Te>=50) depends on Tbg (2.73 vs 5 K), the T prior and varies 0.1-0.8 between variants; (e) lnZ seed scatter 0.4-1.1 (2.9 for k=22); profile chi2 is the best of the final SMC particles; (f) the single-state rejection at N rests on the HCN-vs-HCO+ pattern of the 10 arcsec lines and drops to dlnZ~5 if either species is removed; (g) p0041 (team-b) finds the N-S abundance contrast only ~2 sigma and a bimodal N temperature, consistent with the poorly constrained N core temperature here.")
json.dump(R,open('/output/report.json','w'),indent=1)
